<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume rose in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume rose in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications rose 36.4 percent in the week ended January 3, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages advanced 37.6 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages rose 35.9 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 37.6 percent to 375.5 from 272.8 the previous week.</p>
<p>The purchase index climbed 32.0 percent to 206.9 in the latest survey from 156.8 in the previous week.  </p>
<p>Change in Number of Applications Expressed as a Percent</p>
<p>Week ended Jan 3	 One Week    Four Weeks	One Year</p>
<p>Mortgage applications     Ago	  Ago		 Ago</p>
